emscripten: the default number of domains is the program's (link time).

The runtime reserves the minor heaps of all the possible domains at
startup, which emscripten's mmap allocates and clears: 16 MB in wasm32,
256 MB in wasm64 with the default of 128.  The runtime, built once for every
program, gets the default from caml_emcc_max_domains: 1 (this weak
definition), or the value a program linked with threads defines (compat.c).
OCAMLRUNPARAM's d= still sets it.

--- a/runtime/caml/domain.h
+++ b/runtime/caml/domain.h
@@
-#ifdef ARCH_SIXTYFOUR
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+extern int caml_emcc_max_domains;
+#define Max_domains_def caml_emcc_max_domains
+#elif defined(ARCH_SIXTYFOUR)
 #define Max_domains_def 128
--- a/runtime/startup_aux.c
+++ b/runtime/startup_aux.c
@@
 static struct caml_params params;
 const struct caml_params* const caml_params = &params;
+
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+__attribute__((weak)) int caml_emcc_max_domains = 1;
+#endif
